  "changes": [
    "MCP settings read the owning runtime endpoint and show read errors with retry. Removed the fallback that substituted installed skills for failed runtime reads.",
    "Restart, enable/disable and delete share the authenticated API response and refresh path. Explicit backend rejection no longer shows success. Add-server transport settings share common fields and preserve review and service-error diagnostics.",
    "Platform identity is initialized once using existing host signals. Sensor setup and cleanup are owned by a single hook effect; the device view no longer stores a second cleanup handle.",
    "External capability, marketplace skill, knowledge statistics, audit entry and reminder definitions reuse matching backend fields through type-only imports. The five emitted JavaScript outputs are unchanged; all nine checked type boundaries retain bidirectional assignability and the same top-level fields.",
    "Eighteen parameterized behavior cases cover platform detection, sensor stop/unmount cleanup, MCP read retry, rejected and successful mutations with authentication, and three add transports. Two restart source-string assertions are replaced by behavior-level coverage."
  ],
  "validationNotes": [
    "The first MCP-focused run had seven new test failures because the test expected relative URLs while the shared API client uses absolute URLs; assertions now inspect the actual URL pathname.",
    "The first sensor test attempted to spy on a jsdom geolocation getter that does not exist; the fixture now supplies a synthetic navigator. Neither issue was a production regression."
  ],
  "limitations": [
    "Related tests use synthetic fetch, socket and sensor fixtures. No actual external server, geolocation or native sensor permission request was exercised.",
    "Platform host signals are assumed available at React mount. This does not implement dynamic host-bridge injection detection.",
    "MCP read races, account supersession and remote-device masked-configuration round trips are outside the changes verified in this batch.",
